# Slack Integration

This is the `@aesir/integration-slack` package - an independent Slack integration using Bolt framework.

## Package Structure

```
packages/integrations/slack/
├── src/
│   ├── api/           # HTTP routes (events, oauth, routes)
│   ├── client/        # Bolt app factory, WebClient creation
│   ├── db/            # Database schema (slack.*), credential store
│   ├── events/        # Event handling with deduplication
│   ├── messages/      # Block Kit builders, message posting
│   ├── oauth/         # Token management, flow utilities
│   ├── types/         # Config, errors
│   └── main.ts        # Service entry point
├── Dockerfile
└── package.json
```

## Bolt Framework Patterns

### App Creation with PostgreSQL InstallationStore
```typescript
import { createBoltApp } from "@aesir/integration-slack";

const app = await createBoltApp({
  db,
  logger,
  socketMode: true, // for development
});
```

### Event Handling
Events use deduplication via event_id to prevent duplicate processing:
```typescript
import { createEventHandler } from "@aesir/integration-slack";

const handler = createEventHandler({
  deliveryStore,
  logger,
});

// Returns null for duplicates
const result = await handler.handleEvent(payload);
```

### Message Posting with Block Kit
```typescript
import { sendApprovalRequest, buildApprovalBlocks } from "@aesir/integration-slack";

await sendApprovalRequest(client, {
  type: "approval_needed",
  taskId: "ABC-123",
  prUrl: "https://github.com/org/repo/pull/42",
  title: "Review needed",
  summary: "Changes ready for review",
}, channelId);
```

## Critical Patterns

### Event Deduplication
- Slack may deliver events multiple times
- Use `event_id` (or generated ID for block_actions) for deduplication
- ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING for atomic duplicate detection
- Return null/skip for duplicate events

### Bot Message Filtering
Filter out bot's own messages to prevent loops:
```typescript
if (event.subtype === "bot_message" ||
    event.subtype === "message_changed" ||
    event.subtype === "message_deleted") {
  return; // Skip
}
```

### 3-Second Rule
Slack expects acknowledgment within 3 seconds:
- Acknowledge immediately, process asynchronously
- Fire-and-forget pattern for event callbacks
- Use async handlers that don't block acknowledgment

### Threading
Maintain conversation context:
```typescript
const threadTs = event.thread_ts || event.ts;
await client.chat.postMessage({
  channel,
  thread_ts: threadTs,
  text: "Reply in thread",
});
```

## Credential Storage

- Database schema: `slack.*` (separate from Linear/GitHub)
- Credentials keyed by `team_id` + `enterprise_id` (composite unique)
- Encryption via `CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY` environment variable
- Bolt's InstallationStore interface backed by PostgreSQL

### Credential Store Usage
```typescript
import { createSlackCredentialStore } from "@aesir/integration-slack";

const store = createSlackCredentialStore({ db, logger });
await store.storeInstallation(installation);
const cred = await store.fetchInstallation({ teamId: "T123" });
```

## Error Handling
```typescript
import { SlackError } from "@aesir/integration-slack";
throw new SlackError("INT_SLACK_API", "Failed to post message", { cause: err });
```

All errors extend `AppError` with `INT_SLACK_*` error codes.

## Connection Modes

### Socket Mode (Development)
- Requires `SLACK_APP_TOKEN` (xapp-...)
- No public URL needed
- Set `SLACK_MODE=socket`

### HTTP Mode (Production)
- Uses `SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET` for request verification
- Requires public URL for event delivery
- Set `SLACK_MODE=http`

## Running Locally

```bash
# Set env vars
export SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
export SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=xxx
export SLACK_CLIENT_ID=xxx
export SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=xxx
export SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-...  # for socket mode
export SLACK_MODE=socket
export DB_HOST=localhost
export DB_PORT=5432
export DB_NAME=aesir
export DB_USER=aesir
export DB_PASSWORD=password
export CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)

# Run migration
pnpm --filter @aesir/integration-slack migrate

# Build and start service
pnpm --filter @aesir/integration-slack build
node packages/integrations/slack/dist/main.js

# Or use dev mode
pnpm --filter @aesir/integration-slack dev
```

## Testing

```bash
# Run all tests
pnpm --filter @aesir/integration-slack test

# Run single test file
pnpm --filter @aesir/integration-slack test path/to/file.test.ts

# Watch mode
pnpm --filter @aesir/integration-slack test --watch
```

## Don't

- Don't respond to Slack more than 3 seconds after event delivery
- Don't process duplicate events (check event_id first)
- Don't respond to bot_message, message_changed, message_deleted subtypes
- Don't import from `packages/integrations/src/slack/` (use `@aesir/integration-slack`)
- Don't skip encryption for tokens (always use `CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY`)
- Don't add Slack-specific logic to `@aesir/integrations` package (belongs in Slack package)
- Don't block event acknowledgment with long-running operations
